  "aiContextParagraph": "The political discourse surrounding the potential vice-presidential candidacy for the next administration has recently focused on Sufmi Dasco Ahmad, who currently serves as the Deputy Speaker of the Indonesian House of Representatives. Various regional branches of the Gerindra party, including those in Central Papua, have officially expressed their support for his nomination. This movement has gained momentum with endorsements from certain DPD RI senators and political figures from other parties who suggest that he is well-positioned to maintain political and economic stability. Observers and political analysts note that his reputation for reliability in executive program implementation makes him a strong contender within the party's internal selection process. Alongside him, other senior Gerindra figures such as Sugiono and Ahmad Muzani are also being discussed in the broader conversation regarding the party's strategic options for the upcoming leadership cycle.",
